<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
      THE ROOT MENU ONLY.

      The OASIS app inside Odoo is TRANSFERS and REPLENISHMENT — not the whole
      suite. An earlier revision put three server actions here that embedded
      the Intelligence, Operations and Command Center consoles in an iframe.
      That shipped the entire product into a window inside Odoo, where it
      competed with Odoo's own navigation and gave away every module to anyone
      who installed the connector. Deleting those menus was not enough on its
      own — the client action stayed registered and callable by RPC until the
      method and its assets were removed too.

      What belongs in Odoo is the part an Odoo user does in Odoo: review what
      OASIS proposes, and approve it into native documents. The intelligence
      that produced those proposals stays outside, which is what is being sold.

      Each feature module hangs its own section under this root, so a client
      who installs only one sees only that one. An OASIS app with nothing under
      it means no feature module is installed.
    -->
    <menuitem id="menu_oasis_root" name="OASIS" sequence="60"
              web_icon="oasis_connector,static/description/icon.png"/>
</odoo>
